Main Board PCB file (textual summary / placement guide)

File: main_board.kicad_pcb
KiCad 9 - human-readable PCB description

Board outline: 50.0 mm x 40.0 mm (rectangle)
Layer count: 2 (Top/Bot)
Keepouts:
- Wi-Fi/BT antenna (ESP32-S3 module): keepout circle 12 mm radius around module antenna area on top layer
- 4G antenna U.FL footprint at rear edge with 6 mm keepout

Placement (recommended coordinates, origin at lower-left):
- U1 ESP32-S3-WROOM-1U: center-left area (X=12mm, Y=25mm)
- J1 CAMERA_24: top edge near center (X=25mm, Y=39mm), keep flat cable exit to top
- J2/J3 DISPLAY connectors: right edge (stacked) near top and mid (X=48mm, Y=30mm / Y=22mm)
- J4 4G_UART + U.FL: rear-right corner (X=46mm, Y=6mm)
- J5 NFC I2C: bottom-left corner (X=6mm, Y=6mm) keep antenna area away from metal
- J6 I2C_EXP: bottom edge near center
- J7/J8 PDM_MIC connectors: top-left and top-right corners respectively (for head mic harness)
- J9 POWER_BUS (JST 6-pin): bottom edge center (X=25mm, Y=2mm)
- POGO pad area: front center edge (X=25mm, Y=40mm) with three 2.5mm circular pads spaced 7.5mm

Zone fills:
- Top copper pour: GND
- Bottom copper pour: BAT+ return as needed

Notes:
- Place decoupling capacitors near ESP32 module power pins (0.1uF + 4.7uF ceramics)
- Place ferrite bead on 3.3V rail input from power board for isolation
- Route high current to 4G area on bottom layer with wide 2.5mm traces
- Use thermal relief for ground via stitching; include 4-6 vias near module.

DRC notes:
- Minimum track width: 0.25 mm for signals, 1.0 mm for 5V high current traces to ML307C
- Via diameter: 0.6 mm
- Mounting: no mounting holes (small robot board)

This is a textual representation of the PCB; import into KiCad and create footprint placements accordingly.
